WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.612
Step seven applies the plan
against the fake, twice.

2
00:00:03.612 --> 00:00:05.897
You read the scope and the repository,

3
00:00:05.897 --> 00:00:10.024
build a client for the apply task on
the fake tenant, and send the plan.

4
00:00:10.024 --> 00:00:12.313
The first run sends four requests.

5
00:00:12.313 --> 00:00:16.137
The second sends none, because
everything already matches.

6
00:00:16.137 --> 00:00:18.687
That's what makes the
apply safe to re-run.

7
00:00:18.687 --> 00:00:22.038
Then list the policies whose
names start with C A oh.

8
00:00:22.038 --> 00:00:24.945
Every C A oh fifteen
and C A oh thirty-seven

9
00:00:24.945 --> 00:00:28.450
policy is enabled for
reporting but not enforced.

10
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.050
That's report-only, in Graph's words.

11
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:36.015
And C A oh oh one, a user policy
that blocks legacy authentication,

12
00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:38.263
stays enabled and untouched.

13
00:00:38.263 --> 00:00:41.470
The code changes only the
policies its files name.
